		<title type="html"><![CDATA[GPS Performance]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4849&amp;p=35613#p35613"><![CDATA[
I've had a MD-UV390 for about three years and have never been impressed by it's GPS reception. It does work, but only if I go outside. Laying the radio with the screen facing skyward seems to help. It was the same way with the ghastly factory firmware, it worked...sort of.<br><br>Cut to yesterday, when I received a second MD-UV390. Shockingly, GPS reception is vastly superior to the older one! Attached is a shot of both radios, indoor, same firmware and both turned on simultaneously for just a few minutes. Has TYT greatly improved their design, or is my original one a dud? The two radios perform absolutely identically in every other way.<br><br>Anyhow, I'm really happy to have a MD-UV390 with<em class="text-italics"> useful </em>GPS and wonder if anybody else has ever seen this big of a discrepancy in performance. Just curious.<br><br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2839&amp;sid=0cae1731b417ae9d635fb16c6ebb59a1" class="postimage" alt="gps.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4063">KC6WOG</a> — Fri Feb 07, 2025 1:35 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
